# Example ReRDMFT input file: LiH, 6-31G, GNOF (two coupling subspaces), FULL_OPTIMIZATION with
# CHOLESKY TRUE: the macro-iteration loop runs on Cholesky vectors of the two-electron integrals
# (Utils/CholeskyEri.h) -- ADAM orbital rotations act on the vectors (O(Nchol n^3)), integral
# elements are evaluated on demand, no dense n^4 tensor is kept in the loop. Compare
# lih_gnof_full_optimization.inp (same system, dense integrals): the converged energies agree to
# the decomposition threshold (CHOLESKY_THRESHOLD, default 1e-10). NON_REL and X2C run in one
# execution.
NELEC 4
BASIS lih-6-31g.gbs
NON_RELATIVISTIC TRUE
X2C TRUE
FUNCTIONAL GNOF
PNOF_SUBSPACES 2
PNOF_COUPLING 2
CHOLESKY TRUE
FULL_OPTIMIZATION TRUE

GEOMETRY
Li  0.000000   0.000000   0.000000
H   0.000000   0.000000   1.594900
END
